;; The module _functools (queue 459, the user's decision of 2026-11-19, as 227's thin _pickle; py-design-1122): functools.py
;; imports reduce, cmp_to_key, partial, Placeholder, _PlaceholderType and _lru_cache_wrapper from _functools, each after
;; its own pure definition, and test_functools runs its C classes only when the module imports. reduce and cmp_to_key are
;; Modules/_functoolsmodule.c's of CPython 3.14.10 (py-design-1122): built-in functions, so a C class's attribute does not
;; bind as a method (TestReduceC, TestCmpToKeyC), _functools_reduce_impl's iteration and messages, cmp_to_key's
;; functools.KeyWrapper (keyobject: its cmp and obj, tp_call making a new wrapper, tp_richcompare calling cmp and comparing
;; its result with 0, no tp_hash beside tp_richcompare: unhashable, DISALLOW_INSTANTIATION, the obj member and its
;; __text_signature__ "(obj)"). The rest stays thin: each other name is functools' pure twin, through a module __getattr__
;; read while functools.py runs (the name is already defined when its import asks for it). A pass among test_functools'
;; C classes of partial and the LRU cache says nothing about a C functools.


